WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.152 --> 00:00:02.460
(bright theme music)

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:05.060
- Here's a tip guaranteed to make life

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.120
all a little more beautiful.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.950
- From artist, Helen Dealtry,

00:00:08.950 --> 00:00:10.420
you've gotta watch this.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.140
- A journal or a sketchbook
is a really good way

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:15.320
to start sort of pulling
these things together

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.150
and forming your own styling,

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.023
getting to know yourself and over time,

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.290
you'll get used to doing something,

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.610
maybe like a mood board.

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:27.750
This is something that I begin
before I start any project.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:30.600
And usually, I'm creating for a client

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.730
or I'm doing a set of paintings,

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:34.710
so it could be like eight paintings.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:36.660
And I know that before I begin

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.320
I really wanna get my palette started.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:41.170
I wanna get excited about
what I'm gonna be painting.

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.170
So I start gathering

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.750
and I start collecting

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.740
and I start laying things down.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.730
We're not actually going to be
painting any of these things

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:51.450
but we want to build the foundation

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.580
and figure out a color
palette and get inspired.

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:57.580
And the way I typically work is by

00:00:57.580 --> 00:01:01.720
moving around the board
with color and form

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:05.090
and just placing things so
that they please me visually,

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.540
'cause I'm the only one seeing this.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.110
And it's just so that when
you come in, in the morning,

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.730
it gets you sort of excited,
it gets you sort of,

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:16.990
the brain starts sparking with ideas.

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:18.060
- I love Helen.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:21.250
Chip and Joanna, where
can I get more of Helen?

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:23.980
- She hosts Art In Bloom
on Magnolia Network,

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:26.650
where she shares the
making of her beautiful

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.250
original creations.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:29.083
- I love it.

00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:31.532
(bright music)

